course: dictionary
lesson: 7233
title: Who helps us get better?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A physiotherapist is a health worker who helps people move better and get stronger after an injury, an illness or an operation. Everyday talk often shortens the word to «physio».
explain: Context tells you what the job involves. «A physiotherapist gives exercises to bend and strengthen the arm a bit more each week.» The clues are bend, strengthen and each week, so the physiotherapist helps a hurt arm get back to working well, bit by bit.
explain: Read the whole sentence, not just the first half. «Doing extra does not speed healing and can strain the healing arm.» Even if you think more is always better, the text says extra exercise does not make the arm heal faster. Strain means to hurt by pushing too hard, so follow the plan you are given.
explain: A second sentence shows the job really helps. «Physiotherapy really can help back pain.» Notice the two words: a physiotherapist is the person, and physiotherapy is the treatment they give.
fact: A physiotherapist is a health worker who helps people move better and get stronger.
fact: Physiotherapists use exercises, massage and stretches to help people recover.
fact: «Physio» is a short, everyday name for a physiotherapist or for physiotherapy.
fact: Physiotherapists help people after an injury, an illness or an operation, such as a footballer or a grandparent after a hip operation.
fact: Physiotherapy is the treatment; a physiotherapist is the trained person who gives it.
exercise: «A physiotherapist gives exercises to bend and strengthen the arm a bit more each week.» What is the physiotherapist's job here? | *Helping the arm move better and get stronger | Taking the arm off | Cooking meals for the family | Selling bracelets
exercise: Sam says doing extra exercises will heal his arm faster. What does the text say? | Healing only happens at night | Physiotherapists never give exercises | *Doing extra does not speed healing and can strain the arm | Extra exercise always makes healing faster
exercise: What is «physio» short for? | Physical education teacher | *Physiotherapist | Dentist | Pharmacist
test: After a hip operation, a grandparent needs to walk again. Who helps them get stronger? | A shop assistant | A bus driver | A magician | *A physiotherapist
test: According to the text, what really can help back pain? | Fake bracelets | *Physiotherapy | Doing nothing at all | Magnetic bracelets
exam: Which best describes a physiotherapist? | A person who sells bracelets | Someone who only checks teeth | A teacher who gives maths homework | *A health worker who helps people move better and get stronger after an injury
